---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { products } from '../../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Products" description="Explore WebMAKER, TagMAKER and VideoMAKER, and see their current development status." path="/products/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">The PlayMAKER toolkit</p><h1>Tools for every<br />part of the game.</h1><p class="section-lede">Three distinct products, one open direction. Current availability is shown with each tool.</p></div></section>
  <section class="page-section"><div class="shell">
    {products.map((product) => <article class="product-detail" id={product.slug}>
      <div class="detail-art"><img src={product.image} alt={`${product.name} artwork`} width="340" height="340" loading="lazy" /></div>
      <div class="detail-copy"><span class="badge">{product.status} · {product.statusDetail}</span><h2>{product.name}</h2><p class="tagline">{product.tagline}</p><p>{product.description}</p><ul>{product.features.map((feature) => <li>{feature}</li>)}</ul><div class="detail-links"><a class="button button-primary" href={`/products/${product.slug}/`}>Explore {product.name} ↗</a>{product.repoUrl && <a class="text-link" href={product.repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository ↗</a>}</div></div>
    </article>)}
    <div class="callout"><p>WebMAKER 0.1.1 is public with a reusable club starter, an illustrated tutorial and a Windows Studio installer. The Nerone club pilot remains available separately.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="cta-band"><div class="shell cta-inner"><div><h2>See how the tools fit.</h2><p>Explore planned data exchange and current limits.</p></div><a class="button" href="/ecosystem/">View ecosystem ↗</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
